course, and so that people can see how it was made. Being public does not
make it free to reuse.

You may read this code, and run it to look at how it works. Course staff at
ANU may copy, run and keep it for marking and academic-integrity checks.

Without the author's written permission, you may not copy it, in whole or
in part, into another project; adapt it, or have an AI coding assistant
reproduce or imitate it from this repository; or redistribute or deploy it
as your own. That includes coursework.

To ask for permission, email u8321477@anu.edu.au and say what you'd like
to use and why. Permission counts only when it comes from that address or
from the author's GitHub account (passionleader).

Third-party assets keep their own licences, listed in
client/public/assets/CREDITS.md (most are CC0).

One file in this repository is not covered by the terms above:
client/src/spaces/osmscape-data.ts holds road, building and tree positions
derived from OpenStreetMap data, so it is © OpenStreetMap contributors and
available under the Open Database Licence (ODbL 1.0),
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Anyone may copy and use that
file under the ODbL's terms (credit OpenStreetMap, and share any adapted
version of it under the same licence).
